CODV gunplay rules (original)
  rust/codv-core and data/weapons.json are original work: the genre's common
  ideas (fire rate, hip and aim-down-sights spread, bloom, view kick, range
  damage falloff, regenerating health) with CODV's own code and values. They
  are the interim gunplay until phase F3 drives weapons with weapon_iw4.

Project structure
  CODV follows the layout and conventions of SK8V by becaring (Apache-2.0),
  https://github.com/becaring/SK8V: a ScriptHookV ASI host, a Rust runtime
  behind a versioned C ABI, pinned upstreams and a resumable player-side
  setup with an ownership manifest. Some build and setup scripts are adapted
  from SK8V's (by way of the sibling DOGV and FIGHTV projects). The GTA
  collision code reused from SK8V is listed above.

GTA reference data (verification only, not redistributed)
  tools/check-natives.py checks native hashes against alloc8or's
  gta5-nativedb-data; tools/check-data.py checks weapon, clip, clipset and
  sound names against DurtyFree's gta-v-data-dumps. Neither is shipped. The
  weapons, animations and sounds used in game are GTA's own, loaded from the
  player's installation.
